    "# Tutorial 01 — Histograms, event weights, and Data/MC comparisons\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is the **entry point** to the C2ST/DCTR project.\n",
    "\n",
    "Before training a neural network to compare Data and Monte Carlo (MC), we first need to be\n",
    "comfortable with the ordinary one-dimensional Data/MC plots that the C2ST generalizes.\n",
    "\n",
    "The goals are:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. understand what a histogram represents;\n",
    "2. understand why MC events carry weights;\n",
    "3. distinguish **raw event counts** from **predicted weighted yields**;\n",
    "4. understand the statistical uncertainty of a weighted histogram;\n",
    "5. load the real DY validation-region samples using the same framework used by the C2ST code;\n",
    "6. make Data/MC plots with the full configured background composition;\n",
    "7. compare MC **before** and **after** the nominal DY correction;\n",
    "8. understand the difference between **physical normalization** and **shape normalization**;\n",
    "9. inspect negative MC weights and effective MC statistics;\n",
    "10. connect these plots to the motivation for a multivariate C2ST.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## How to use this notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "Cells marked **Exercise** contain work for the student.\n",
    "\n",
    "For written questions, add your answer in the empty Markdown cell immediately below the question.\n",
    "\n",
    "A complete reference solution is provided separately in:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "01_histograms_weights_datamc_solutions.ipynb\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Try the exercises before opening the solution notebook.\n",
   ]
  },
