  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ea5cfd76",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Question 6.1\n",
    "\n",
    "For MC, why can `len(df)` and `df[\"weight\"].sum()` differ dramatically?\n",
    "\n",
    "For Data, why are they expected to be equal?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1447efc1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Reference answer.** `len(df)` counts stored rows; `sum(weight)` estimates the physical weighted\n",
    "yield. MC rows have non-unit event weights, while Data uses unit weights, so for Data the selected row\n",
    "count and weighted yield coincide."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a4f2a547",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 7. A small helper for selecting one channel\n",
    "\n",
    "The loader has already restricted us to the DY validation region, so downstream plotting only needs to\n",
    "choose the lepton channel.\n",
    "\n",
    "This helper keeps the plotting cells readable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8475f3c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def select_channel_tables(tables, channel):\n",
    "    mc = []\n",
    "    data = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    for label, df in tables.items():\n",
    "        selected = df[df[\"channel\"] == channel]\n",
    "\n",
    "        if label in cfg.DATA_PROCESSES:\n",
    "            data.append(selected)\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            mc.append((selected, label))\n",
    "\n",
    "    return mc, data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5247303a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 8. Unweighted real MC is not the physical prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "Before making the correct Data/MC plot, deliberately make an unweighted MC plot.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is useful because it shows why simply counting simulated rows is misleading."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a4c2592c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Exercise 8.1 — Unweighted MC composition\n",
    "\n",
    "For the `2mu` channel and `mli_ll_pt`, plot the raw number of rows for each MC process.\n",
    "\n",
    "Do **not** compare this plot quantitatively with Data. Its purpose is to inspect the generated sample\n",
    "composition, not the physical prediction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f0f6bba6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "mc_2mu, data_2mu = select_channel_tables(tables, \"2mu\")\n",
    "\n",
    "bins_llpt = np.linspace(0, 200, 41)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "for df, label in mc_2mu:\n",
    "    if len(df) == 0:\n",
    "        continue\n",
